cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CASIMIR, please cite it as below. The manuscript describing the model is not yet published, and this file will be updated with the article reference once it is."
type: software
title: "CASIMIR: An Open Pediatric Model for Whole-Body T1-Weighted MRI Anatomy Segmentation"
abstract: "CASIMIR (Child Anatomy Segmentation In MRI with Increased Robustness) is a 2D nnU-Net v2 model that segments six visceral organs and seven skeletal structures in pediatric and young-adult whole-body T1-weighted MRI, paired structures labeled by side."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fjhorvath/casimir"
url: "https://huggingface.co/fjhorvath/casimir"
keywords:
  - medical imaging
  - MRI
  - whole-body imaging
  - image segmentation
  - pediatrics
  - nnU-Net
